From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: a 64-bit exe without relocations keeps its allocations low (5954)

ntdll: a 64-bit exe without relocations keeps its allocations low

A 64-bit exe flagged DYNAMIC_BASE and HIGH_ENTROPY_VA had the low address
space freed, so its heap, GlobalAlloc and VirtualAlloc went above 4 GB.
An exe whose relocations are stripped cannot be relocated: it is not
ASLR-compatible whatever its flags say, and on Windows its allocations
stay low. NSIS's 64-bit installers and uninstallers are such exes, and
scripts doing pointer arithmetic with IntOp (32-bit) crashed on the
sign-extended pointer: foobar2000's uninstaller walking
PendingFileRenameOperations (System.dll, read at FFFFFFFFFExxxxxx; qa5
Store walk 2026-10-22). The low reserve is now kept for those. An exe
with relocations keeps upstream's high-entropy allocations.
Gate: test/relocheap-gate.sh (the same probe with and without
IMAGE_FILE_RELOCS_STRIPPED); mutant SG_MUTANT_RELOCHEAP.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 565af84..5136290 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4599,8 +4599,17 @@ void virtual_set_large_address_space(void)
         if (is_wow64())
             user_space_wow_limit = ((main_image_info.ImageCharacteristics & IMAGE_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE) ? limit_4g : limit_2g) - 1;
 #ifndef __APPLE__  /* don't free the zerofill section on macOS */
+        /* an exe without relocations is not ASLR-compatible whatever its flags say: it keeps its
+           allocations low, as on Windows. NSIS's 64-bit installers are such (DYNAMIC_BASE and
+           HIGH_ENTROPY_VA with relocations stripped), and scripts doing pointer arithmetic with
+           IntOp (32-bit) crashed with a heap above 2 GB: foobar2000's uninstaller walking
+           PendingFileRenameOperations (qa5 Store walk 2026-10-22) */
         else if ((main_image_info.DllCharacteristics & IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_HIGH_ENTROPY_VA) &&
-                 (main_image_info.DllCharacteristics & IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_DYNAMIC_BASE))
+                 (main_image_info.DllCharacteristics & IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_DYNAMIC_BASE)
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_RELOCHEAP
+                 && !(main_image_info.ImageCharacteristics & IMAGE_FILE_RELOCS_STRIPPED)
+#endif
+                )
             free_reserved_memory( 0, (char *)0x7ffe0000 );
 #endif
     }
